jobs.description:
What will you be doing?
As a Production Employee, you play an important role in the preparation and packaging of food products. Together with your team, you help keep production running efficiently while making sure quality and safety standards are met. Your attention to detail and proactive attitude contribute to a smooth workflow and a well-organized production environment.

Your responsibilities include:

• Packing and preparing finished products so they are ready for shipment;
• Setting up, operating, and monitoring production equipment during the manufacturing process;
• Performing quality checks on products, packaging, and labeling to ensure all requirements are met;
• Keeping the work area clean, tidy, and compliant with hygiene and safety regulations;
• Collaborating with colleagues and supervisors to achieve production goals and meet daily schedules.

Functie-eisen:
What are we looking for?

• You have a good command of either English, Dutch, or both, allowing you to understand procedures and work safely within a production environment;
• You enjoy working in different locations and are open to being assigned to various production facilities throughout the region;
• You are flexible regarding working hours and can work rotating shifts, including mornings, afternoons, evenings, and nights for 16 to 32 hours per week;
• You are eager to learn new skills, adapt quickly to changing tasks, and become familiar with different production equipment;
• You have an eye for detail, value quality, and actively contribute to a clean, organized, and safe workplace.

Are you a hands-on worker with an eye for detail? Do you enjoy working in a dynamic environment where you can truly make a difference? Then this is your chance to join a leading international company in the world of excavators!

What are you going to do?
As a Logistics Employee, you are an essential link in the logistics operation. You ensure smooth goods flows and make sure everything is processed neatly, safely, and efficiently.

Your tasks:

- Loading, unloading, receiving, and inspecting goods (possibly using a forklift)
- Entering goods into the system and storing them correctly
- Collecting orders and delivering them on time to the correct location
- Ensuring safety, quality, and order in the warehouse
- Actively contributing ideas for process improvements
- Collaborating with colleagues from various departments

What do we offer?
- A varied job at a renowned international organization;
- A competitive salary between € 17 and € 18,50 gross an hour;
- Travel allowance of €0.25 per km;
- Immediate participation in our pension scheme;
- Access to the online Adecco Academy – an online platform with 150+ e-learnings and courses.

Where will you work?
At Hitachi Construction Machinery (Europe), you will be part of the logistics team behind powerful and innovative construction machines. From the warehouse in Amsterdam, we ensure that parts, materials, and machines are delivered worldwide in perfect condition.

What do we ask?
- Good command of Dutch or English;
- Experience in logistics;
- Experience as a forklift driver – Note: a valid certificate is required;
- Good physical condition;
- Accurate working style and adherence to procedures.

Are you interested?
Are you ready to take the next step in your career? Apply now! More questions you can always call Bastiaan Roele by phone 06-52367235

Mandarin Oriental Conservatorium is looking for a Chef de Partie to join our Ottolenghi team.Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional. Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world's most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences.

Functie-eisen:
As Chef de Partie, you will be responsible for the following duties:
• You will be supervising the day-to-day operation of a designated section within the kitchen, overseeing all aspects of food production;
• Delivering highest levels of quality and precision, preparing dishes in line with recipes and standards;
• Maintaining highest levels of hygiene and cost control;
• You will act as a role model and mentor to the junior members in the kitchen brigade, guiding and supporting them in their development.Yotam Ottolenghi's restaurants are renowned London eateries known for vibrant, Middle Eastern-inspired dishes, offering everything from delis to full restaurants, featuring seasonal ingredients, bold flavors, and colorful displays, perfect for breakfast, lunch, and dinner.As Chef de Partie we expect from you: 
• Recent/current experience in the same position to that of Chef de Partie for at least two years;
• A passionate and quality-driven approach to cooking;
• Teamwork, being able to work closely with 6-8 chefs on shift;
• Experience in inspired Middle Eastern cooking cuisine;
• Good knowledge of English language (written and spoken);
• Familiar with hygiene code and HACCP regulations;
• Ability to work evenings and weekend shif

Safran Aircraft Engine Services Brussels is a subsidiary of Safran Aircraft Engines, based at Brussels Airport (Zaventem & Steenokkerzeel, Belgium), specialized in the inspection, maintenance and repair (MRO) of the advanced LEAP jet engines that power the latest generation of the Airbus A320NEO & Boeing B737MAX narrow body families. The company is a key player in the integrated CFM international MRO network. With more than 75 years of experience, and up to 20 international Part 145 certifications (EASA/ FAA/ CAAC/ …), Safran Aircraft Engine Services Brussels is recognized as a worldwide center of expertise in the air transport industry. More than a 100 airlines, lessors, private aircraft operators and MRO partners have entrusted their engines to our company. We employ over 600 highly skilled, passionate and enthusiastic employees.

We are currently looking for a Security Manager.

Your role within the team:

• Access Control Management: you participate in access control management using a computerized system, primarily responsible for creating and assigning standard access profiles. In collaboration with the security teams, you ensure that only authorized individuals have access to the appropriate areas according to their defined access profile;
• Camera Security: you are responsible for camera surveillance at the sites, including managing and monitoring video surveillance systems, including verifying their proper functioning;
• Supervision of Security Staff: as a security manageryou oversee the G4S security personnel working at the sites. You conduct performance evaluations and provide training and development on company guidelines and procedures;
• Translation of Security Standards and Policies: together with the HR Director you ensure that the Group's security standards and policies are translated into practical guidelines at the local level. You also collaborate with facility management to develop local security policies;
• Collaboration with External Partner: you closely collaborate with external partners such as G4S, government agencies and security services to ensure site security and compliance with legal requirements and regulations in the field of security;
• Risk Management: you regularly conduct risk analyses to identify and evaluate potential threats. Based on this, you proactively develop strategies and measures to minimize risks and strengthen site security;
• Emergency Planning and Response: you contribute to the development and implementation of emergency plans and procedures. You coordinate emergency response and ensure effective communication and collaboration with relevant stakeholders and emergency services;

Your profile:

• You have a minimum of 5 years of experience in a similar role, preferably in a production environment.
• You have a Bachelor's degree or equivalent through experience.
• Knowledge and experience in privacy legislation and security practices are a must.
• You have experience in identifying security risks and implementing appropriate security measures.
• Capable of accurately analyzing and structure information and have the ability to convey complex information in a simple and understandable way.
• You have a proactive and practical approach of identifying and solving security issues.
• Good command of English, Dutch and French.

